  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task was to solve the differential equation y''(t) - 2y'(t) + 10y(t) = 0 and display its general solution.\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows the Wolfram Alpha homepage with an empty search input field.\n\n**Screenshot 2:** Shows the equation \"y''(t) - 2 y'(t) + 10 y(t) = 0\" correctly entered into the Wolfram Alpha search box.\n\n**Screenshots 3-5:** Show the results page from Wolfram Alpha, which displays:\n- **Input:** y''(t) - 2 y'(t) + 10 y(t) = 0\n- **ODE classification:** second-order linear ordinary differential equation\n- **Differential equation solution:** y(t) = c₁ eᵗ sin(3t) + c₂ eᵗ cos(3t)\n- Plots of sample individual solutions and a sample solution family\n\n## Mathematical Verification\nThe characteristic equation is r² - 2r + 10 = 0, giving roots r = (2 ± √(4-40))/2 = 1 ± 3i. The general solution is therefore y(t) = eᵗ(C₁cos(3t) + C₂sin(3t)), which matches the displayed solution y(t) = c₁ eᵗ sin(3t) + c₂ eᵗ cos(3t) (with constants relabeled). The solution shown is mathematically correct.\n\n## Response Consistency\nThe result response accurately describes what is shown in the screenshots: the equation was solved and the general solution y(t) = c₁ eᵗ sin(3t) + c₂ eᵗ cos(3t) was displayed, along with the equivalent form eᵗ(c₁cos(3t) + c₂sin(3t)).\n\n## Conclusion\nThe differential equation was successfully entered into Wolfram Alpha, and the general solution was computed and displayed on screen. Both parts of the task (solving the equation and displaying the general solution) were accomplished.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
